          "sessionID": "ses_10",
          "messageID": "msg_02",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Semver is actually a promise about *when* things are allowed to break, not a guarantee that nothing will. The version format is `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`: patch releases are bug fixes, minor releases add backward-compatible features, and major releases are explicitly allowed to make breaking changes. Going from `2.x` to `3.x` is a major bump, so socket.io 3.0 is free to change or remove APIs — and it did (the `io.sockets`/namespace API changed significantly between v2 and v3). These build errors are exactly that: code written against the old API surface."
        },
        {
          "id": "prt_02d",
          "sessionID": "ses_10",
