          "sessionID": "ses_10",
          "messageID": "msg_04",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "It's the opposite: minor and patch bumps are the ones that *promise* not to break your code — that's what makes them safe to auto-update. Major bumps are the one category semver explicitly reserves for breaking changes; that's the signal it exists to give you. In socket.io's case, v3 replaced `io.sockets.sockets` (an object) with `io.sockets.sockets` as a `Map`, and `.clients(callback)` was replaced by `.fetchSockets()` returning a promise. Let's fix these call sites one at a time."
