          "messageID": "msg_08",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Caret is the opposite of a pin — `^2.1.0` means \"any version compatible with 2.1.0,\" which npm interprets as `>=2.1.0 <3.0.0`. That's why `npm ls` shows 2.7.3 actually installed even though `package.json` says `^2.1.0`: npm picked the latest 2.x release available when it was last installed. If you actually wanted an exact pin, you'd drop the caret entirely: `\"express\": \"2.1.0\"`."
        },
