          "sessionID": "ses_10",
          "messageID": "msg_10",
          "type": "text",
          "text": "They're not meant to match exactly — they answer different questions. `package.json` says what *range* of versions is acceptable (`^2.1.0`). `package-lock.json` records the *exact* version that was resolved and installed within that range, so every teammate and CI run gets the identical 2.7.3 instead of npm re-resolving \"any 2.x\" separately each time and potentially getting different patch versions. That's the whole point of a lockfile: the range lives in `package.json`, the resolved reality lives in the lock."
        },
        {
